  "info": {
    "title": "GoPOS API",
    "description": "\u003Ch2\u003EAuthorization (Beta)\u003C/h2\u003E\n\n\u003Cstrong\u003EWorks if You generate credentials on website Settings\u003C/strong\u003E\n\nTo fetch \u003Cstrong\u003Etoken\u003C/strong\u003E used for auth you need to send POST request to /oauth/token endpoint. Request should include params as\n\n- grant_type = organization\n\n\n- client_id = ...\n\n- client_secret = ...\n\n- organization_id = {organizationId}\n\nwhere \u003Cstrong\u003E{organizationId}\u003C/strong\u003E is the ID of the organization the API request applies to\n\n\u003Cstrong\u003Etoken\u003C/strong\u003E should be passed as \u003Cstrong\u003EAuthorization\u003C/strong\u003E header with value \u003Cstrong\u003EBearer {token}\u003C/strong\u003E\n\n\u003Cstrong\u003Etoken\u003C/strong\u003E gives You permission \u003Cstrong\u003EONLY\u003C/strong\u003E to selected \u003Cstrong\u003EOrganizations\u003C/strong\u003E\n\n\u003Ch2\u003EAuthorization (Deprecated)\u003C/h2\u003E\n\n\u003Cstrong\u003EWorks only for if You have credentials for grant_type=password by mail from IT department\u003C/strong\u003E\n\nTo fetch \u003Cstrong\u003Etoken\u003C/strong\u003E used for auth you need to send POST request to /oauth/token endpoint. Request should include params as\n\n- grant_type = password\n\n\n- client_id = ...\n\n- client_secret = ...\n\n- username = ...\n\n- password = ...\n\n\u003Cstrong\u003Etoken\u003C/strong\u003E should be passed as \u003Cstrong\u003EAuthorization\u003C/strong\u003E header with value \u003Cstrong\u003EBearer {token}\u003C/strong\u003E\n\n\u003Ch2\u003EHow to import this API into Postman?\u003C/h2\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EFollow these steps to import the API from the provided URL into Postman:\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Col\u003E\n    \u003Cli\u003E\n        \u003Cstrong\u003EDownload the API Documentation:\u003C/strong\u003E\n        \u003Cul\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003EOpen your browser and navigate to: \u003Ca href=\"https://app.gopos.io/v3/api-docs/Public%20API\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EGoPOS public API description\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003ESave the API documentation in either .txt or .json file format.\u003C/li\u003E\n        \u003C/ul\u003E\n    \u003C/li\u003E\n    \u003Cli\u003E\n        \u003Cstrong\u003EImport the API into Postman:\u003C/strong\u003E\n        \u003Cul\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003EOpen Postman.\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003ENavigate to the \u003Cstrong\u003ECollections\u003C/strong\u003E tab.\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003EClick on \u003Cstrong\u003EImport\u003C/strong\u003E and select the file you downloaded in the previous step.\u003C/li\u003E\n        \u003C/ul\u003E\n    \u003C/li\u003E\n    \u003Cli\u003E\n        \u003Cstrong\u003EConfigure Import Settings:\u003C/strong\u003E\n        \u003Cul\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003EAfter selecting the file, click on \u003Cstrong\u003EView Import Settings\u003C/strong\u003E located at the bottom left side of the panel.\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003Cli\u003EAdjust the configuration settings as follows:\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003Cul\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENaming requests:\u003C/strong\u003E Fallback\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESet indent character:\u003C/strong\u003E Space\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EParameter generation:\u003C/strong\u003E Example\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EFolder organization:\u003C/strong\u003E Tags\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EInclude auth info in example requests:\u003C/strong\u003E True\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EEnable optional parameters:\u003C/strong\u003E True\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EKeep implicit headers:\u003C/strong\u003E False\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EInclude deprecated properties:\u003C/strong\u003E True\u003C/li\u003E\n                \u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EAlways inherit authentication:\u003C/strong\u003E False\u003C/li\u003E\n            \u003C/ul\u003E\n        \u003C/ul\u003E\n    \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EBy following these steps, you will successfully import the API into Postman with the desired settings.\u003C/p\u003E\n\n\u003Ch3\u003EAdditional Information\u003C/h3\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EFor more details about orders api, visit the GoPOS Public workspace on Postman:\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\"https://www.postman.com/gopos/workspace/gopos-public/overview\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EGoPOS Public Workspace on Postman\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\n",
